#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0099 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "ASTDY and AENDY are real ADaM OCCDS variables (adam-occds-1-0 and 1-1, both Num), so this is a genuine offending record. The shipped Scope is Data_Structures.Include [BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, OCCURRENCE DATA STRUCTURE] (Fix #274, ruling M2-D7) - it restores the OCCDS half the rule's own sheet Domains cell names AND moves the rule off the retired Scope.Classes channel. The harness derives the structure set from the class=OCCDS declaration through ScenarioDeclaredScopeProvider.effectiveDeclaredStructure, and AEDECOD additionally makes the column heuristic say OCCDS on its own. ONE expansion, ONE violation at row 1. Under the previous Scope.Classes.Include [BASIC DATA STRUCTURE] the harness reported the dataset out of scope. CDISC-AD0099 deliberately keeps BDS - its own sheet says so."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 ASTDY=10 AENDY=5
dataset ADAE class=OCCDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AEDECOD type=Char
col ASTDY   type=Num
col AENDY   type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | 10 | 5
